{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Duplicate/RCA disposition before close.\n\nStep 0(a): tracker sweep for `dict(os.environ) pytest fixture secrets environment leak` found closed canonical sibling ticket `dumbstruck-wonderful-xiphosuran` with the same title, same seven fixture surfaces, same plan, and same acceptance criteria as this ticket. Step 0(b): no report version in this duplicate; using created_at floor gives origin/main floor a22257e7d10e3d079ee676cbb38d2b39811d0fd5, with no later changes to the seven suspect fixture files. Step 0(c): worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/credleak-fixtures` at e768151d680f7295bfd37424cec31946b88d0ab8 (= origin/main).\n\nProven root cause: this ticket is not a new live defect. It is a duplicate of already-landed `dumbstruck-wonderful-xiphosuran`: prior RCA showed seven decorated fixtures copied the complete insertion-ordered `os.environ` into values rendered by pytest on unrelated failures. Current origin/main follows the established fix pattern: each fixture now builds an explicit mutable allowlist instead of copying arbitrary ambient keys (`tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_materialize_probe.py:91`, `test_autodeploy_fetch_secrets.py:102`, `test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py:123`, `test_autodeploy_health_gate.py:118`, `test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py:106`, `test_observability_exit.py:69`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli.py:58`).\n\nProof/replication: focused minimal-parent run over both sentinel-rendering security tests and all affected fixture consumers returned `72 passed, 1 skipped in 97.73s` using `env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin \"$PWD/.venv/bin/python\" -m pytest -q ...`. The original long-trace sentinel leak no longer reproduces. Construct sweep: an AST scan of all `tests/**/*.py` found no `@pytest.fixture` returning `dict(os.environ)`, `os.environ.copy()`, or a nested alias to either; `test_autodeploy_materialize_certbot.py::_make_box` remains outside scope as a plain helper per the canonical RCA, and broader subprocess-env carrier work remains on `antiutopic-toadyish-goldfinch`.\n\nDefect origin/Gerrit: canonical fix is Gerrit Change 1851, commit aa41c2e45ad10da6296f6b642d0eed9e9ba76d6e, reachable from origin/main with trailer `rebar-ticket: 3402-7143-2e14-4d1a`; prior ticket records LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments, and merged CI run 32111971923. Because this ticket is a duplicate rather than an independent defect fix, the durable origin is the `duplicates` edge to `dumbstruck-wonderful-xiphosuran`, not a new `caused_by` edge."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788231696576300659,"uuid":"4f63b7b4-08ab-47a9-b528-03f7a2e25b97"}